<title>CANADA: CWB details Prairie elevator space, railcar unload.</title>
<headline>CWB details Prairie elevator space, railcar unload.</headline>
<dateline>WINNIPEG 1997-07-02</dateline>
<text>
<p>Vacant space in Canadian Prairie primary grain elevators fell to 29 percent in the week ended June 29 while railcar unloads exceeded targets, the Canadian Wheat Board said.</p>
<p>The 29 percent elevator vacancy rate was down from 31 percent on June 22, the Board said.</p>
<p>Manitoba had the most space available at 36 percent, Alberta had 33 percent space available and Saskatchewan had 25 percent of space available.</p>
<p>Vancouver unloaded 3,231 railcars versus the 3,300 target. Prince Rupert unloaded 1,417 railcars versus the 1,300 target.</p>
<p>Thunder Bay unloaded 3,641 railcars versus the 3,420 target.</p>
<p>((Gilbert Le Gras, Winnipeg Reuters bureau 204 947 3548))</p>
